{
  "name": "Calpine daily gas nomination to HPL scheduler",
  "change": "Replace Calpine's daily phone call plus emailed Word nomination with one structured electronic nomination and a standing 'same as prior day' rule, so HPL acts only on changes.",
  "reason": "The 10 minutes a day saved rest on steps the mail does not show: a daily phone call (mentioned in only 4 of about 23 nominations, and 169.eml says 'will call if there are any changes'), no-change days (nothing shows volumes repeating, and REVISED resends, monthly totals of 79-85 and force-majeure claims show they change), and HPL re-keying the Word document (never shown); the 30-a-month rate also ignores that weekend nominations come in one Friday message (1330.eml), and two critics have already rejected this same work for these reasons.",
  "research": "Look in the schedulers' own mailboxes (Robert Lloyd, Juliann Kemp) for what HPL does with each Calpine nomination, such as replies to Ricky Archer, keying errors or corrections, or rework caused by revisions, and for nomination contents showing how often volumes repeat; that could support a smaller weekday-only saving for the scheduler's keying step."
}

{
  "name": "Back-dated MTM valuations for counterparties' auditors",
  "today": "Counterparties must show their auditors a third-party valuation of their derivative deals with Enron, and Confirmations (Joe Hunter, Ellen Wallumrod) must supply it. Confirmations has no system that values the deals. So each request is emailed to five or six regional risk desk heads (Gossett, Keiser, Love, Giron, McLaughlin, Baumbach). Each desk head forwards it to someone on the desk, who runs a mini-book for that counterparty as of a past date, often the year end, and sends back the regional total and detail. In the example in the mail, the answer then goes back through the desk head. The regional answers are then added together. The mini-book also shows Delta/Vol figures, which have to be blacked out before the result can go to the counterparty. The work stalls in the fan-out: one request becomes five or six forwards and five or six mini-book runs, and Confirmations has to wait for every desk to answer.",
  "change": "Give Confirmations a read-only report of MTM value by counterparty and past date, across all regions and without Delta/Vol, so it can answer auditors without asking the risk desks.",
  "explanation": "Finish the back-dated valuation view that Confirmations already plans ('EnTelligence', with back-dated curves). Until it is ready, set up a standing read-only query or report for Confirmations: enter a counterparty short name and an as-of date, and get the MTM value and deal detail for every region, with the Delta/Vol columns left out. Confirmations staff run it themselves and send the result to the counterparty. Desk heads and risk analysts are no longer involved, nothing has to be blacked out, and nobody has to add up the regional replies.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/240.eml",
      "quote": "Please forward to Ellen Wallumrod the MTM valuation(mini-book) for all \nCoEnergy Trading Company deals as of Dec 31, 2000."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/214.eml",
      "quote": "Can you provide MTM values as of Dec 29, 2000, for the short name of CROSS \nTIMBERS."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/137.eml",
      "quote": "Two more counterparties need MTM values for Dec. 29, 2000."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/136.eml",
      "quote": "The following are the totals for Tudor BVI and Ospraie.  The total MTM value \nfor the West Desk are as follows."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
      "quote": "We do not have access to \nany system that values these deals, but are looking to get the on-line \n\"EnTelligence\" built so that it carries back-dated curves that will allow us \nto complete these requests without taking up a Risk person's time and without \nhaving to black out information (Delta/Vol) that is included in a mini-book.",
      "note": "Confirmations itself names the cause (no valuation access), the steps the change removes (risk staff time, blacking out Delta/Vol) and the fix it wants."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
      "quote": "Until we can get EnTelligence built to our specifications, \nwe'll need to continue to go to the different desks to provide Mark-to-Market \nvaluations for a Counterparty's portfolio.",
      "note": "Each request goes to all the regional desks. This email went to six desk heads."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/137.eml",
      "quote": "Please provide the total MTM value for that date within your region.",
      "note": "Each region answers separately, and the totals then have to be added up."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/240.eml",
      "quote": "If you can export into \nexcel and forward by e-mail, that would be appreciated.",
      "note": "The desk staff run the mini-book, export it to Excel and email it back."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/136.eml",
      "quote": "Detail can be found in the attachment.",
      "note": "The analyst (Carole Frank) answers the desk head, who forwards the answer on. That is one more relay step per region."
    }
  ],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": {
    "count": 2,
    "per": "week",
    "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
    "quote": "we recieve several \nper week"
  },
  "minutes": 50
}

