{
  "name": "Monthly GLO/EGM gas-for-crude swap tickets",
  "today": "HPL sells gas to the Texas General Land Office (GLO) and Enron Gas Marketing (EGM) receives crude in exchange. In March 2001 Bryce Baxter set up a four-ticket accounting treatment that has to be redone by hand every month before flash. Someone zeroes the price on that month's HPL sale to GLO. They work out the gas value (index x firm volume) and enter it as demand charges on the HPL-to-ENA and ENA-Wellhead tickets. They enter the prior month's crude value on the ENA-to-EGM demand ticket. Julie Meyers did this for January and February 2001, but the March deal was copied from January's with the price still on it, and March onward was never completed. A price she had zeroed was also put back. By August and October 2001, Megan Parker was rebuilding March to May by hand and asking Risk to update demand fees for prior months and book August and September crude.",
  "change": "Book the GLO swap once as term deals with a zero-price GLO sale and formula-priced demand tickets, so the only monthly input is the crude value.",
  "explanation": "Risk/Logistics would book the HPL sale to GLO once for the whole term at zero price, keeping the volume. That removes the monthly zeroing and the risk of copying a priced ticket. The HPL-to-ENA and ENA-Wellhead demand tickets would also be booked once, with the demand amount set by formula as firm volume times the month's gas index, so the system calculates it when the index posts. The ENA-to-EGM demand ticket would be booked once for the term. Each month Settlements would enter the prior month's crude value on it in one place and check the result before flash.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/175.eml",
      "quote": "This will require the following steps be taken monthly as this deal goes forward:"
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/175.eml",
      "quote": "547201 & 591307 has been zeroed out.  679847 & 679848 have been created between ENA & HPLC.  679859 has been created for the sale to EGM from ENA Wellhead."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/28.eml",
      "quote": "I have already sent an email to risk to update the demand fees for the prior months and to book Aug and Sept crude."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/175.eml",
      "quote": "The price on the sale from HPL to GLO will need to be zeroed out monthly.",
      "note": "The monthly zeroing step, which a term deal at zero price would remove."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/175.eml",
      "quote": "The index for the gas value is available shortly after the 1st of the month, and since the volume is firm, there shouldn't be a problem calculating the value.",
      "note": "The gas-side demand charge is a plain calculation (index x firm volume), so a formula can do it."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/175.eml",
      "quote": "Deal 640685 for March 01 production:  per Daren Farmer (in the Audit field in Sitara), this was copied from deal #547201.",
      "note": "The March ticket was copied from January, and Settlements had to ask for it to be rebooked."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/83.eml",
      "quote": "Julie Meyers was told how to create the deals and she completed January and February, except for one small part, but March forward was never completed.",
      "note": "The monthly hand steps were missed from March on, which left months of catch-up work."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/83.eml",
      "quote": "Julie zeroed this out, but O'Neal put it back.",
      "note": "A hand-zeroed price was undone, which shows how fragile the monthly edits are."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/83.eml",
      "quote": "Here is a preliminary list of what needs to be done to finish out the transactions for March, April and May.",
      "note": "In August, Settlements was rebuilding three months of tickets by hand."
    }
  ],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": {
    "count": 1,
    "per": "month",
    "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/175.eml",
    "quote": "This needs to be done monthly prior to flash"
  },
  "minutes": 39
}

{
  "name": "Nightly check that every book and post ID is marked official",
  "today": "Every night each book administrator must mark each of their books and post IDs official in the risk system, including books with no position, because credit otherwise picks up the previous day's position. Books left unofficial go on a daily list that goes to Sally Beck and is reviewed weekly by Rick Buy. To catch misses, the West gas desk (Darron Giron's group of five administrators) uses an Excel macro written by Dutch Quigley: someone types in the date and the portfolio and book codes, runs it, and compares the official books it returns with the post IDs that should be official. Giron had to remind the group that the last person to finish must run it every night, because Jason Wolfe had been doing it 'most nights'. Regional controllers also get a sheet each night confirming that all books are official. The older check, which compared risk-system positions with Excel position reports, misses post IDs that have no net position. That is how the West-NW-GDL book was missed on a Friday in October 2000, which led to emails between Moscoso, Gossett and Giron.",
  "change": "Have the risk system email each book administrator and controller, every evening, the list of their post IDs not yet marked official, including flat ones.",
  "explanation": "IT would add a scheduled report to the risk system. It would hold each administrator's list of active post IDs and, at a set time each evening, email each administrator and their regional controller the ones not yet marked official, including those with zero position. It would resend until the list is empty. Administrators would no longer open the macro, type in the date and codes, and check the results. Controllers would get the same report instead of a separate verification sheet. Flat books would no longer slip through and end up on the list reviewed by Beck and Buy.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/533.eml",
      "quote": "Let's make sure we are doing this every night.  I think Jason has been running the official post id macro most nights, but we need to have the last person finished do it every day."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/582.eml",
      "quote": "Use it to make sure all your postid's that need to be, are officialized each night."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/533.eml",
      "quote": "All regional controllers will receive a sheet at the end of the night, verifying that all books are officialized."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/582.eml",
      "quote": "To run this file all that has to be done is enter the date and have the Portfolio and Book CD entered in also.",
      "note": "The macro is run by hand each night after typing in the date and codes. A scheduled report would remove this step."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/580.eml",
      "quote": "This one requires a comment in all post-id's to pull in only those.",
      "note": "The desks were patching the macro themselves, which is extra upkeep a system report would not need."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/595.eml",
      "quote": "If a postid has a net position and is not officialized, it will be caught using this procedure.  It will not, however, if the postid does not have a position.",
      "note": "The position-based check misses flat post IDs. The new report would list them too."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/595.eml",
      "quote": "This list goes to Sally Beck and is reviewed at the end of each week by Rick Buy.",
      "note": "A miss is escalated to senior management, which led to an email chain between Moscoso, Gossett and Giron."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/401.eml",
      "quote": "If a book is not officialized, it picks up the previous day's position.",
      "note": "Why flat books must also be marked official each night, so the report has to include them."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/492.eml",
      "quote": "I believe this is all of the Enovate/EMW books that are officialized each night.",
      "note": "One desk's Enovate books alone list 20 post IDs to check each night."
    }
  ],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": {
    "count": 1,
    "per": "working day",
    "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/533.eml",
    "quote": "Let's make sure we are doing this every night."
  },
  "minutes": 6
}

