{
  "name": "Nightly El Paso (EPE) model vs. CARP reconciliation entry",
  "today": "Since July 2001 the Portland real-time shift must, at the end of each trading day, tie out the El Paso model with the CARP report and log the El Paso totals in a reconciliation spreadsheet on the shared drive, explaining any variances. The sheet must be filled in even when nothing differs, because Houston reads an empty sheet as a sign that nobody ran CARP. The file is kept per month (July01, aug01 folders). In the first 8 days of July there were no variances at all, yet the entry is still made by hand every night. On 10 July Bill Williams had to remind the night traders that the sheet had been left blank the night before. The reconciliation itself works well: the July checkout with Settlements took about five minutes instead of the five days spent the month before. So the remaining cost is the nightly manual entry, mostly on nights with nothing to report.",
  "change": "Have a scheduled job compare the El Paso model with the CARP report each night, log the totals and a 'no variance' stamp itself, and flag only the variances for the trader.",
  "explanation": "Real Time Trading Support would set up a job or macro that runs after CARP finishes. It reads the day's El Paso model totals and the CARP report, compares them, and writes the totals and the result into the month's reconciliation file, creating the next month's file when needed. A timestamp shows Houston that CARP was run. If there is a variance, the job emails the shift a list of the hours and deals that differ, and the trader only has to write the explanation. On nights with no variance, nobody has to open the sheet, and a blank sheet can no longer be caused by a forgotten entry.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/williams-w3/sent_items/417.eml",
      "quote": "Even if there are no variances, please complete the July EPE Reconciliation sheet going forward."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/williams-w3/sent_items/304.eml",
      "quote": "El Paso totals should be logged in the reconciliation model (m://electric/epe/epe01/aug01/epe reconciliation model) and all variances explained."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/williams-w3/sent_items/418.eml",
      "quote": "I just skimmed through the first 8 days of this month, and we show no variances between the Real Time El Paso model and our CARP report."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/williams-w3/sent_items/417.eml",
      "quote": "Houston will assume that no one ran the CARP if the sheet has no entries.",
      "note": "The entry is required even on nights with nothing to report, only as proof that CARP was run. An automatic stamp would provide that proof."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/williams-w3/sent_items/417.eml",
      "quote": "Great job on the cong last night but the EPE reconciliation sheet was not done.",
      "note": "The manual entry gets skipped on busy nights, and the manager has to follow up."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/williams-w3/sent_items/304.eml",
      "quote": "El Paso model must tie out with CARP when trading day is done. Check spreadsheet formulas.",
      "note": "Every trading day the trader has to compare the model with CARP by hand. This is the step the job would do."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/williams-w3/sent_items/315.eml",
      "quote": "Our checkout with Kathy and the Settlements group took approximately five minutes, as opposed to the five days we spent sorting it out last month.",
      "note": "The month-end checkout is already quick, so the saving claimed here is only the nightly entry, not the month-end work."
    }
  ],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": {
    "count": 1,
    "per": "day",
    "file": "corpus/williams-w3/sent_items/304.eml",
    "quote": "El Paso model must tie out with CARP when trading day is done."
  },
  "minutes": 5
}

{
  "name": "Researching HPLC-ENA intercompany accrual variances",
  "change": "Have Sitara create the mirror side of every HPLC-ENA intercompany deal automatically, and add a daily intercompany nomination tie-out",
